IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nt-interpretation-time`

-- Tests of the time module.
-- Every expected value is written here from the text of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory), not from the module's output.
-- The weekday of each date was worked out by hand from 1 January 2026, which is a Thursday.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVETH A LIST OF `Public holiday`
`no public holidays` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A `Public holiday`
`a whole-day public holiday on 2 February 2026` MEANS
    `Public holiday` WITH `the day of the public holiday` IS Date 2 2 2026
                        , `the public holiday is part of a day only` IS FALSE

GIVETH A `Public holiday`
`a part-day public holiday on 2 February 2026` MEANS
    `Public holiday` WITH `the day of the public holiday` IS Date 2 2 2026
                        , `the public holiday is part of a day only` IS TRUE

§ `Section 17 "calendar month": the last day of the month commencing on a day`

-- Limb (a): the end of the day before the corresponding day of the next named month.
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS Date 14 2 2025
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS Date 31 1 2025
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 31 12 2025) EQUALS Date 30 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 29 1 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2024
-- Limb (b): no corresponding day, so the end of the next named month.
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 31 1 2024) EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 31 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 30 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 29 1 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 31 3 2025) EQUALS Date 30 4 2025
-- The boundary between the limbs: 28, 29 and 30 January of a common year.
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar month": the last day of the calendar month commencing at the beginning of` (Date 28 1 2025) EQUALS Date 27 2 2025

§ `Section 28(1): a period dating from a day, act or event is reckoned exclusive of that day`

-- Periods in days: the first day counted is the next day and the last day is N days after the given day.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the first day counted in a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 2 1 2026
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 1 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 28 2 2024) 2 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2024)
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 28 2 2025) 2 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2025)
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 30 12 2025) 3 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2026)

-- Periods in months: calendar months one after another, the first commencing at the beginning of the day after the given day.
-- One month from 15 January 2025: the month commences on 16 January and ends at the end of 15 February.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)
-- One month from 31 January 2024: the month commences on 1 February and ends at the end of 29 February.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025: January 2026 and then February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- One month from 30 April 2025: the month commences on 1 May and ends at the end of 31 May.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 30 4 2025) 1 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 5 2025)
-- One month from 28 February 2025: the month commences on 1 March and ends at the end of 31 March.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 28 2 2025) 1 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
-- Two months from 29 January 2025: the first month commences on 30 January and, there being no 30 February, ends at the end of February;
-- the second commences on 1 March and ends at the end of March.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 29 1 2025) 2 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
-- Three months from 31 January 2025: February, March, April.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 31 1 2025) 3 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 30 4 2025)
-- Twelve months and a month over the end of a year.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 15 12 2025) 2 `months` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2026)

-- Periods in years: a year is a period of 12 months.
-- Three years from 16 July 2025: 36 calendar months, the first commencing on 17 July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 16 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025 and from 1 September 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2030)
-- One year from 29 February 2024: 12 calendar months from 1 March 2024, ending at the end of February 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- One year from 28 February 2023: 12 calendar months from 1 March 2023, ending at the end of February 2024, which has 29 days.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 28 2 2023) 1 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- One year from 30 January 2024: the first of the twelve months commences on 31 January and, there being no 31 February, ends at the end of February;
-- the other eleven are March 2024 to January 2025, so the year ends at the end of 31 January 2025 and not on 30 January 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 30 1 2024) 1 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2025)
-- One year from 15 January 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 15 1 2025) 1 `years` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2026)

-- Not covered: the Act is silent on weeks, and says nothing about a period of no days or of part of a day.
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 2 `weeks` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 `days` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 0 `months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1): the last day of a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 1.5 `days` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 28(1) and (1A): is the given day counted?`

#ASSERT `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period` `dating from a given day, act or event` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period` `ending at, with or on a given day, act or event` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (1A): the given day, act or event is counted in the period` `expressed in some other way` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period of 5 days ending on 10 January includes the 10th: it begins on the 6th.
#ASSERT `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on` (Date 10 1 2026) 5 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 6 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on` (Date 10 1 2026) 1 `days` EQUALS JUST (Date 10 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on` (Date 10 1 2026) 1 `months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on` (Date 10 1 2026) 1 `weeks` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 28(1A): the first day of a period ending on` (Date 10 1 2026) 0 `days` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 28(2): the last day falls on a day of rest`

-- 31 January 2026 is a Saturday, 1 February a Sunday and 2 February a Monday.
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 31 1 2026) `no public holidays`
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 1 2 2026) `no public holidays`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 2 2 2026) `no public holidays`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 30 1 2026) `no public holidays`))
-- A public holiday is a rest day; a public holiday that is part of a day is not.
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 2 2 2026) (LIST `a whole-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`)
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 28(2): the day is a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 2 2 2026) (LIST `a part-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`)))
-- The thing may be done on the first following day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday.
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is` (Date 31 1 2026) `no public holidays` EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is` (Date 31 1 2026) (LIST `a whole-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`) EQUALS Date 3 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is` (Date 31 1 2026) (LIST `a part-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`) EQUALS Date 2 2 2026
-- A last day that is not a day of rest is the last day.
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the last day on which the thing may be done, for a period whose last day is` (Date 30 1 2026) `no public holidays` EQUALS Date 30 1 2026
-- A public holiday on the Friday and the Monday around a weekend.
#ASSERT `s 28(2): the first day, on or after the day, that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday` (Date 30 1 2026) (LIST `a whole-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`) EQUALS Date 30 1 2026

-- The worked cases, with the rule of section 28(2) applied to the last day.
-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026: the last day is Saturday 31 January, so the thing may be done on Monday 2 February.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 30 `days` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025: the last day is Saturday 28 February 2026, so the thing may be done on Monday 2 March.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 31 12 2025) 2 `months` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024: Thursday 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 31 1 2024) 1 `months` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- One year from 29 February 2024: Friday 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 29 2 2024) 1 `years` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2025)
-- Three years from 16 July 2025: the last day is Sunday 16 July 2028, so the thing may be done on Monday 17 July.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 16 7 2025) 3 `years` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 17 7 2028)
-- Five years from 15 January 2025: Tuesday 15 January 2030.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 15 1 2025) 5 `years` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2030)
-- Five years from 1 September 2025: the last day is Sunday 1 September 2030, so the thing may be done on Monday 2 September.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 1 9 2025) 5 `years` `no public holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 9 2030)
-- Not covered stays not covered.
#ASSERT `s 28(1), (2): the last day on which a thing may be done within a period dating from` (Date 1 1 2026) 1 `weeks` `no public holidays` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 17: business day, calendar year, financial year`

#ASSERT (NOT (`s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (Date 31 1 2026) `no public holidays`))
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (Date 1 2 2026) `no public holidays`))
#ASSERT `s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (Date 2 2 2026) `no public holidays`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (Date 2 2 2026) (LIST `a whole-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`)))
#ASSERT `s 17 "business day": the day is a business day` (Date 2 2 2026) (LIST `a part-day public holiday on 2 February 2026`)
-- The calendar year commencing on 1 January 2024 ends on 31 December 2024 (a year is a period of 12 months).
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar year": the last day of the calendar year of` 2024 EQUALS Date 31 12 2024
#ASSERT `s 17 "calendar year": the last day of the calendar year of` 2025 EQUALS Date 31 12 2025
-- The financial year ending on 30 June 2025 commences on 1 July 2024.
#ASSERT `s 17 "financial year": the first day of the financial year ending on 30 June of` 2025 EQUALS Date 1 7 2024
-- A year is 12 months from the 1st: it ends on the last day of the 12th month, and on 30 June 2025 the financial year ends.
#ASSERT `s 17 "year": the last day of consecutive years, the first commencing at the beginning of` (Date 1 7 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 30 6 2025
-- Several months: one calendar month after another, each commencing at the beginning of the day after the previous one ends.
-- One month commencing 1 February 2024 ends at the end of 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `s 17 "month": the last day of consecutive calendar months, the first commencing at the beginning of` (Date 1 2 2024) 1 EQUALS Date 29 2 2024
-- Two months commencing 31 January 2025: the first has no corresponding 31 February and ends at the end of February; the second commences on 1 March and ends at the end of 31 March.
#ASSERT `s 17 "month": the last day of consecutive calendar months, the first commencing at the beginning of` (Date 31 1 2025) 2 EQUALS Date 31 3 2025
-- Three months commencing 1 February 2025: February, March and April.
#ASSERT `s 17 "month": the last day of consecutive calendar months, the first commencing at the beginning of` (Date 1 2 2025) 3 EQUALS Date 30 4 2025
-- Three months commencing 15 November 2025: to 14 December, to 14 January, to 14 February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 17 "month": the last day of consecutive calendar months, the first commencing at the beginning of` (Date 15 11 2025) 3 EQUALS Date 14 2 2026

§ `Section 30: age`

-- Born on 29 February 2008: the anniversary in a year that is not a leap year is 28 February; in a leap year it is 29 February.
#ASSERT `s 30(2), (3): the day on which the anniversary of the birth occurs in` (Date 29 2 2008) 2009 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2009)
#ASSERT `s 30(2), (3): the day on which the anniversary of the birth occurs in` (Date 29 2 2008) 2012 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2012)
#ASSERT `s 30(2), (3): the day on which the anniversary of the birth occurs in` (Date 15 6 2000) 2018 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2018)
#ASSERT `s 30(2), (3): the day on which the anniversary of the birth occurs in` (Date 28 2 2008) 2009 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2009)
-- Section 30(3) speaks of a subsequent year: the year of the birth and earlier years are not covered.
#ASSERT `s 30(2), (3): the day on which the anniversary of the birth occurs in` (Date 29 2 2008) 2008 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(2), (3): the day on which the anniversary of the birth occurs in` (Date 29 2 2008) 2007 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person attains an age on the relevant anniversary.
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the day on which a person attains the age` (Date 29 2 2008) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the day on which a person attains the age` (Date 15 6 2000) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 6 2018)
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the day on which a person attains the age` (Date 15 6 2000) 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the person has attained the age on` (Date 29 2 2008) 18 (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the person has attained the age on` (Date 29 2 2008) 18 (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the person has attained the age on` (Date 29 2 2008) 18 (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(1): the person has attained the age on` (Date 15 6 2000) 0 (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 29: the 24 hour clock`

#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 0 9 0 5 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 9, `minutes after the hour` IS 5)
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 2 3 5 9 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 23, `minutes after the hour` IS 59)
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 0, `minutes after the hour` IS 0)
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 1 2 3 0 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 12, `minutes after the hour` IS 30)
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 0 0 0 5 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 0, `minutes after the hour` IS 5)
-- Minutes must be less than an hour; the text speaks of a time of day, so 24 hours and over are not covered.
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 1 2 6 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 2 4 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 1 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST (`Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 10, `minutes after the hour` IS 0)
#ASSERT `s 29: the time after midnight for four digits` 12 3 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 28(3) to (5)`

#ASSERT `s 28(3): a reference to time is read as a reference to` EQUALS "standard time declared by section 4 of the Standard Time Act 2005"
#ASSERT `s 28(4), (5): a time expression is read as` `from time to time` EQUALS `the thing existing or having effect at any time`
#ASSERT `s 28(4), (5): a time expression is read as` `for the time being` EQUALS `the thing existing or having effect at that time`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 28(4), (5): a time expression is read as` `from time to time` EQUALS `the thing existing or having effect at that time`))

§ `Fixtures for commencement`

GIVETH A `Time of day`
`midnight` MEANS `Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 0, `minutes after the hour` IS 0

GIVETH A `Time of day`
`half past two in the afternoon` MEANS `Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 14, `minutes after the hour` IS 30

GIVETH A `Moment`
`midnight at the start of 1 July 2023` MEANS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 1 7 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS `midnight`

GIVETH A `Moment`
`the last minute of 30 June 2023` MEANS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 30 6 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS `Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 23, `minutes after the hour` IS 59

GIVETH A `Moment`
`half past two on 1 July 2023` MEANS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 1 7 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS `half past two in the afternoon`

GIVETH A `Moment`
`one minute before half past two on 1 July 2023` MEANS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 1 7 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS `Time of day` WITH `whole hours after midnight` IS 14, `minutes after the hour` IS 29

GIVETH A `Moment`
`midnight at the start of 15 July 2023` MEANS `Moment` WITH `the day of the moment` IS Date 15 7 2023, `the time of day of the moment` IS `midnight`

§ `Section 5: the day on which an Act commences`

#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (`on a particular day` (Date 1 7 2023)) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2023)
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (`on a day fixed by Gazette notice` (JUST (Date 10 8 2023))) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 8 2023)
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (`on a day fixed by Gazette notice` NOTHING) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Example for subsection (2)(c): on the commencement of another Act, which commences on 1 January 2024.
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (`on the happening of an event` (JUST (Date 1 1 2024))) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2024)
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (`on the happening of an event` NOTHING) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (4): no commencement specified, so the day after the day on which assent is declared.
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 30 11 2022) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 12 2022)
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2023)
#ASSERT `s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 28 2 2024) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- A specified day governs over the assent day.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 5: the day on which an Act or a provision commences` (`on a particular day` (Date 1 7 2023)) (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 1 2023)))

§ `Section 6: proposed laws reserved for the Governor-General`

#ASSERT `s 6: the first day on which a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General has effect` (Date 1 7 2023) (JUST (Date 15 7 2023)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 7 2023)
#ASSERT `s 6: the first day on which a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General has effect` (Date 1 7 2023) (JUST (Date 20 6 2023)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2023)
#ASSERT `s 6: the first day on which a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General has effect` (Date 1 7 2023) (JUST (Date 1 7 2023)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2023)
#ASSERT `s 6: the first day on which a proposed law reserved for the Governor-General has effect` (Date 1 7 2023) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 6A: the moment of commencement`

#ASSERT `s 6A: the moment at which an Act or a provision commences` (Date 1 7 2023) NOTHING EQUALS `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6A: the moment at which an Act or a provision commences` (Date 1 7 2023) (JUST `half past two in the afternoon`) EQUALS `half past two on 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6A: the Act or provision has commenced at` `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023` `the last minute of 30 June 2023`))
#ASSERT `s 6A: the Act or provision has commenced at` `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023` `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6A: the Act or provision has commenced at` `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023` `half past two on 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6A: the Act or provision has commenced at` `half past two on 1 July 2023` `one minute before half past two on 1 July 2023`))
#ASSERT `s 6A: the Act or provision has commenced at` `half past two on 1 July 2023` `half past two on 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 6A: the Act or provision has commenced at` `half past two on 1 July 2023` `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`))

§ `Section 6B: references to commencement`

#ASSERT `s 6B: the commencement of the provisions concerned` (LIST `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`) EQUALS JUST `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6B: the commencement of the provisions concerned` (LIST `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`, `midnight at the start of 15 July 2023`) EQUALS JUST `midnight at the start of 15 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6B: the commencement of the provisions concerned` (LIST `midnight at the start of 15 July 2023`, `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`) EQUALS JUST `midnight at the start of 15 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6B: the commencement of the provisions concerned` (LIST `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`, `half past two on 1 July 2023`) EQUALS JUST `half past two on 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6B: the commencement of the provisions concerned` (LIST `half past two on 1 July 2023`, `one minute before half past two on 1 July 2023`, `midnight at the start of 1 July 2023`) EQUALS JUST `half past two on 1 July 2023`
#ASSERT `s 6B: the commencement of the provisions concerned` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 63B: commencement of subordinate legislation`

#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` (`on a particular day` (Date 1 8 2023)) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2023)
-- Subsection (2) lists a particular day and the happening of an event; a day fixed by Gazette notice is not among them.
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` (`on a day fixed by Gazette notice` (JUST (Date 1 8 2023))) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Example 1 for subsection (2)(b): on the commencement of a section of an Act (here 1 September 2023).
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` (`on the happening of an event` (JUST (Date 1 9 2023))) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2023)
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` (`on the happening of an event` NOTHING) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Subsection (5): the day after the day on which it is made.
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2023)
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 28 2 2023) FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2023)
-- Subsection (6): a rule or by-law not published or to be published on the legislation website commences on the day it is notified in the Gazette.
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 15 3 2023)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2023)
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- A rule or by-law that is published on the website, and a regulation that is not, both take subsection (5).
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 15 3 2023)) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2023)
#ASSERT `s 63B: the day on which subordinate legislation commences` `commencement is not specified or provided for` (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE FALSE (JUST (Date 15 3 2023)) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2023)
-- Subsections (3) and (4): a day before the day it is made, with no express provision in the Act, is of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 63B(3), (4): the provision of subordinate legislation is of no effect` (Date 9 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63B(3), (4): the provision of subordinate legislation is of no effect` (Date 10 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63B(3), (4): the provision of subordinate legislation is of no effect` (Date 9 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 63B(3), (4): the provision of subordinate legislation is of no effect` (Date 11 3 2023) (Date 10 3 2023) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 25(2) to (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served`

#ASSERT `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by prepaid post` (Date 10 3 2023) (JUST (Date 14 3 2023)) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2023)
#ASSERT `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by prepaid post` (Date 10 3 2023) NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by fax` (Date 10 3 2023) NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2023)
#ASSERT `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by fax` (Date 10 3 2023) NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served` `by sending it by fax` (Date 10 3 2023) NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 25(2), (3), (4): the day on which a document is taken to be served` `by leaving it at the recipient's address with someone who appears to be at least 16 years old and to live or be employed there` (Date 10 3 2023) NOTHING FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2023)
