#ASSERT `s 12(a): the thing was in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect` (Date 1 7 2023) NOTHING (Date 1 7 2023)
#ASSERT `s 12(a): the repeal revives the thing` `a thing not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(a): the repeal revives the thing` `anything duly done or suffered under the repealed Act or part` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Section 12(b), (c), (d).
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `the previous operation of the repealed Act or part` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `anything duly done or suffered under the repealed Act or part` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `a right, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under the repealed Act or part` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence against the repealed Act or part` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a penalty, forfeiture or punishment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(b), (c), (d): the repeal affects the thing` `a thing not in force or existing at the time at which the repeal takes effect` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 12, closing words.
#ASSERT `s 12: the thing may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been made` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a right, privilege, obligation or liability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: the thing may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been made` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred in respect of an offence against the repealed Act or part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: the thing may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been made` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of such a penalty, forfeiture or punishment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12: the thing may be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing Act had not been made` `the previous operation of the repealed Act or part` EQUALS NOTHING

